Create a directory in this project called Marketplace. It should then be broken into a frontend and backend folder. Then scaffold two projects. The front end will be a vue frontend that either operates as buildless vue pulled from the web or supports building for full performance. The page will be a sleek dark-mode with vibrant neon accents. Make a home page for waviate script with navigation to helpful pages like the docs and whatever else. Then make a search page where people can search by users, by tags, sort by ratings and so on. all paginated. For anything unimplemented or unwired just leave todo comments. like no need to link this to the backend yet. just clean structure and a good looking scaffolded UI.
When that's done, create the backend project scaffolding. It should have two modes. Serverless and Server but reuse all the same business logic. scaffold the project into a go project that has a validation layer for uploads, a persistence layer for communicating to the DB and reading from it, a controller layer with auth flows or middleware, whatever works best in go, that support common oauth like google, microsoft, etc and a desktop app communication layer that will communicate with the VST via 'open file from browser in this application prompt'. For implementation details like how upload and validation will work or how users will pull marketplace entries from the site to the VST, don't worry about those now. keep this abstract, readable, and modular.
Finally create a db simulation layer that builds out the db on the local machine. this can be in a separate folder from front end and backend. maybe call it persistence. This will have idempotent powershell scripts that install postgres if its not available on the machine, run all one-time scripts in the order they've been made, and so on. make a one-time scripts folder that represents the newest version of the DB to date with no data in it. Then make a data folder that's a bunch of sql scripts you can run to put data into the DB. like manual scripts.